    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0511" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51/1283: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain (Mellon)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-16T18:00:00-05:00">November 16, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>283. Your 328, November 15, 5 p.m. The Department fails to understand the reason
                    for the failure of the British Government to <pb facs="0512" n="422"
                        xml:id="pg422"/> accede to the representations you made on November 12.
                    Immediately upon receipt of the expected official reply telegraph a résumé
                    thereof.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
